<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF offers 400 bln yen 3.0% 20-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF offers 400 bln yen 3.0% 20-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance said on Tuesday it was offering 400 billion yen worth of 3.0 percent 20-year bonds through a price-competitive auction.</p>
<p>The auction will close at 0300 GMT and the results will be announced at 0530 GMT.</p>
<p>The issue date will be April 21, 1997 and the maturity date will be September 20, 2017.</p>
</text>
